2026-10-28T17:39:31.2948140Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015c6TQzKdikyowXkd2b2YQ7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 23,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/23\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"resource/aws_secretsmanager_secret_version: `secret_string_wo_version` documented as Optional but enforced as required when `secret_string_wo` is set\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"## Description\\n\\nThe documentation for [`aws_secretsmanager_secret_version`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs/resources/secretsmanager_secret_version#secret_string_wo_version-2) lists `secret_string_wo_version` as **Optional**:\\n\\n> `secret_string_wo_version` - (Optional) Attribute used to trigger updates when rotating `secret_string_wo`.\\n\\nHowever, in practice, whenever `secret_string_wo` is set, the provider **requires** `secret_string_wo_version` to also be present. Omitting it causes a plan-time error:\\n\\n```\\nError: Missing required argument\\n\\n  with aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.example,\\n  on main.tf line N, in resource \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\\\" \\\"example\\\":\\n\\n\\\"secret_string_wo\\\": all of secret_string_wo,secret_string_wo_version must be specified\\n```\\n\\nThis is because the provider schema internally has `RequiredWith: []string{\\\"secret_string_wo\\\"}` on `secret_string_wo_version`, making it conditionally required \\u2014 not truly optional.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure `aws_secretsmanager_secret_version` with `secret_string_wo` set but **without** `secret_string_wo_version`:\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  secret_id        = aws_secretsmanager_secret.example.id\\n  secret_string_wo = \\\"my-secret-value\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n2. Run `tofu plan` (or `terraform plan`)\\n\\n**Expected:** Plan succeeds (since docs say Optional)\\n**Actual:** Plan fails with `all of secret_string_wo,secret_string_wo_version must be specified`\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe documentation should clearly state that `secret_string_wo_version` is **required when `secret_string_wo` is set**, not simply \\\"Optional\\\". The current wording misleads users into omitting it.\\n\\n## Suggested Fix\\n\\nUpdate the registry documentation at the `secret_string_wo_version` anchor to read:\\n\\n> `secret_string_wo_version` - (Required when `secret_string_wo` is set) Attribute used to trigger updates when rotating `secret_string_wo`. Must always be specified alongside `secret_string_wo`.\\n\\n## Additional Context\\n\\n- Provider version: `hashicorp/aws ~> 6.43`\\n- Related issue: `#44590` (`secret_string_wo_version` also cannot accept ephemeral values \\u2014 a separate but related problem)\\n- This is a documentation-only clarification request; the `RequiredWith` constraint makes the \\\"Optional\\\" label incorrect.\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:02Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-03T16:10:30Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73b35784-c45d-438c-85de-058a3e5d9f9b","uuid":"bda70a40-79c9-4746-97a4-b37dd0bb6a18","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:39:31.289Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 23,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/23\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"resource/aws_secretsmanager_secret_version: `secret_string_wo_version` documented as Optional but enforced as required when `secret_string_wo` is set\",\n  \"body\": \"## Description\\n\\nThe documentation for [`aws_secretsmanager_secret_version`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs/resources/secretsmanager_secret_version#secret_string_wo_version-2) lists `secret_string_wo_version` as **Optional**:\\n\\n> `secret_string_wo_version` - (Optional) Attribute used to trigger updates when rotating `secret_string_wo`.\\n\\nHowever, in practice, whenever `secret_string_wo` is set, the provider **requires** `secret_string_wo_version` to also be present. Omitting it causes a plan-time error:\\n\\n```\\nError: Missing required argument\\n\\n  with aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.example,\\n  on main.tf line N, in resource \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\\\" \\\"example\\\":\\n\\n\\\"secret_string_wo\\\": all of secret_string_wo,secret_string_wo_version must be specified\\n```\\n\\nThis is because the provider schema internally has `RequiredWith: []string{\\\"secret_string_wo\\\"}` on `secret_string_wo_version`, making it conditionally required \\u2014 not truly optional.\\n\\n## Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Configure `aws_secretsmanager_secret_version` with `secret_string_wo` set but **without** `secret_string_wo_version`:\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  secret_id        = aws_secretsmanager_secret.example.id\\n  secret_string_wo = \\\"my-secret-value\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n2. Run `tofu plan` (or `terraform plan`)\\n\\n**Expected:** Plan succeeds (since docs say Optional)\\n**Actual:** Plan fails with `all of secret_string_wo,secret_string_wo_version must be specified`\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\nThe documentation should clearly state that `secret_string_wo_version` is **required when `secret_string_wo` is set**, not simply \\\"Optional\\\". The current wording misleads users into omitting it.\\n\\n## Suggested Fix\\n\\nUpdate the registry documentation at the `secret_string_wo_version` anchor to read:\\n\\n> `secret_string_wo_version` - (Required when `secret_string_wo` is set) Attribute used to trigger updates when rotating `secret_string_wo`. Must always be specified alongside `secret_string_wo`.\\n\\n## Additional Context\\n\\n- Provider version: `hashicorp/aws ~> 6.43`\\n- Related issue: `#44590` (`secret_string_wo_version` also cannot accept ephemeral values \\u2014 a separate but related problem)\\n- This is a documentation-only clarification request; the `RequiredWith` constraint makes the \\\"Optional\\\" label incorrect.\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:02Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-03T16:10:30Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015c6TQzKdikyowXkd2b2YQ7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
